    <field_name>V</field_name>
    <field_msb>1</field_msb>
    <field_lsb>1</field_lsb>
    <rel_range>1</rel_range>
    <field_description order="before"><para>Whether the value last written to <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_selr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link> selects a valid interrupt.</para>
<para>This field is updated if and only if any of the following occur:</para>
<list type="unordered">
<listitem><content>A write that sets <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_selr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link>.S to 1.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content>A write to any of the following registers:<list type="unordered">
<listitem><content><register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_cactiver.xml" state="">IRS_INT_CACTIVER</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_enabler.xml" state="">IRS_INT_ENABLER</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_hmr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_HMR</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_iaffidr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_IAFFIDR</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_pendingr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_PENDINGR</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_priorityr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_PRIORITYR</register_link>.</content>
</listitem></list>
</content>
</listitem></list>
<para>When IDLE is 0, the value of this field is <arm-defined-word>UNKNOWN</arm-defined-word>.</para></field_description>
    <field_description order="after">
      <para>This field resets to 0 to indicate that there was no write to <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_selr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link> that selected a valid interrupt on this IRS since the IRS was reset.</para>
    </field_description>
    <field_values impdef="False">
      <field_value_instance>
        <field_value>0b0</field_value>
        <field_value_description>
          <para>The interrupt selected using <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_selr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link> is not valid.</para>
        </field_value_description>
      </field_value_instance>
      <field_value_instance>
        <field_value>0b1</field_value>
        <field_value_description>
          <para>The interrupt selected using <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_selr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link> is valid.</para>
        </field_value_description>
      </field_value_instance>
    </field_values>
    <field_resets>
      <field_reset reset_type="GIC">
        <field_reset_number>'0'</field_reset_number>
      </field_reset>
    </field_resets>
  </field>
  <field id="fieldset_0-0_0" has_partial_fieldset="False" is_linked_to_partial_fieldset="False" is_access_restriction_possible="False" is_variable_length="False" is_constant_value="False" is_partial_field="False" is_conditional_field_name="False">
    <field_name>IDLE</field_name>
    <field_msb>0</field_msb>
    <field_lsb>0</field_lsb>
    <rel_range>0</rel_range>
    <field_description order="before"><para>A write that sets <register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_selr.xml">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link>.S to 1 is complete when this field is 1.</para>
<para>When this field is 1 and V is 1, a read from <register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_cfgr.xml">IRS_INT_CFGR</register_link> returns values for the selected interrupt.</para>
<para>Following a write to one of the following registers, when this field returns 1, the effects of the write have completed:</para>
<list type="unordered">
<listitem><content><register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_cactiver.xml">IRS_INT_CACTIVER</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_enabler.xml">IRS_INT_ENABLER</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_hmr.xml">IRS_INT_HMR</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_iaffidr.xml">IRS_INT_IAFFIDR</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_pendingr.xml">IRS_INT_PENDINGR</register_link>.</content>
</listitem><listitem><content><register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_priorityr.xml">IRS_INT_PRIORITYR</register_link>.</content>
</listitem></list></field_description>
    <field_description order="after">
      <para>This field resets to 1 to allow initial writes to registers Guarded by this field.
Because there has been no write at reset, a reset value of 1 does not imply that any write to <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_int_selr.xml" state="">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link> to select an interrupt is complete.</para>
    </field_description>
    <field_values impdef="False">
      <field_value_instance>
        <field_value>0b0</field_value>
        <field_value_description>
          <para>The effects of the last write that set <register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_selr.xml">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link>.S to 1 or any write to an interrupt configuration register is not guaranteed to be complete.</para>
        </field_value_description>
      </field_value_instance>
      <field_value_instance>
        <field_value>0b1</field_value>
        <field_value_description>
          <para>The effects of the last write that set <register_link state="ext" id="ext-irs_int_selr.xml">IRS_INT_SELR</register_link>.S to 1 and any writes to interrupt configuration registers are complete.</para>
        </field_value_description>
      </field_value_instance>
    </field_values>
    <field_resets>
      <field_reset reset_type="GIC">
        <field_reset_number>'1'</field_reset_number>
      </field_reset>
    </field_resets>
